{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum","id":925709,"title":"Is there an inspirational works post for the Wraith forum?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-03T22:03:05-07:00","id":925709,"title":"Is there an inspirational works post for the Wraith forum?","content":"Over on the Mage forum they found they were getting so many posts like that that they made a sticky for it. Not sure if that would make sense here, but I'm curious what has been done on the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T11:23:31-07:00","id":925989,"title":"","content":"El Espinazo del Diablo (The Devil's Backbone<br /> The Grudge /Ju on<br /> The Ring/ Ringu<br /> The Sixth Sense<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T16:07:30-07:00","id":926127,"title":"","content":"For video games:<br /> <br /> Grim Fandango-Yes, it's zany and silly at times but at the same time there are concepts in the game that are quite compatible with Wraith and I can see its story being converted into the Wraith universe without much difficultly.<br /> <br /> Murdered: Sole Suspect-I swear the guys behind this one must have cracked open some WtO books because there are aspects that scream Wraith or at least Wraith-inspired.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T16:20:52-07:00","id":926136,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Oddly, I rarely get <i>Wraith</i> inspiration from ghost stories. Weird and random things that inspire me are (but not limited to):</span><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Mad Max films</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><i>The Road</i> (Hillcoat, 2009)</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><i>The Book of Eli</i> (The Hughes Bros., 2010)</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><i>Word War Z: An Oral History of the Zombie War </i> (Brooks, 2006)</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><i>The Hills Have Eyes</i> (any)</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><i>Thirteen Ghosts</i> (either version)</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><i>The Seventh Seal</i> (Bergman, 1957)</span></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","user":"Nazfool","date":". 07-05-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T23:46:17-07:00","id":926294,"title":"","content":"Beetlejuice is up there.<br /> <br /> I think many of the works of Kafka apply.<br /> <br /> What Dreams May Come.<br /> <br /> The Divine Comedy.<br /> <br /> Jacob's Ladder.<br /> <br /> Twilight Zone is appropriate for a lot of kinds of Harrowings.<br /> <br /> The Exorcist.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T03:18:01-07:00","id":926344,"title":"","content":"Poltergeist <br /> Magnetic Rose (short film by Katsuhiro Otomo) <br /> Ghost in the Shell (futuristic possession, anyone?) <br /> Aliens (for Doomslayers) <br /> Alien 3 (the soundtrack)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T22:05:43-07:00","id":926849,"title":"","content":"I'll take that as a no on a post like this existing before. I did try looking for one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Jacob's Ladder, The Seventh Seal, The Sixth Sense--seconded.<br /> <br /> Donnie Darko. Technically a time travel movie, but very Wraith-like thematically. To a lesser extent The Butterfly Effect.<br /> <br /> Most things by Edgar Allen Poe, obviously.<br /> <br /> Never Let Me Go, Remains of the Day. Kazuo Ishiguro is great at both death and regret.<br /> <br /> The Crow--I think? It's so tonally uncanny I can't bring myself to finish it. In a different mood I think I'd like the atmosphere.<br /> <br /> Cheesy as it is, I have to give props to Ghost with Patrick Swayze. I think it is very likely Wraith wouldn't have been conceived without it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T23:19:30-07:00","id":926878,"title":"","content":"Faradn, I agree with all your comments. Crow is definitely a source for Revenants, but also for Wraith in general. &quot;Ghost&quot; is certainly something that can be emulated by the game, and given when it was released, I have to say it had an influence.<br /> <br /> Meet Joe Black is also something I think is very appropriate. Not a good movie, but very good in terms of Wraith. I took many elements of that for the one Wraith chronicle I ran.<br /> <br /> Totally agree on Donnie Darko.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T05:47:23-07:00","id":927005,"title":"","content":"Franklyn <br /> Dark City <br /> Blade Runner <br /> Twelve Monkeys <br /> The Devil's Backbone","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T11:21:30-07:00","id":927187,"title":"","content":"The Frighteners<br /> House on Haunted Hill<br /> The Haunting (Original)<br /> The Changeling (It's a ghost film)<br /> Secrets of the Dead (tv)<br /> Paranormal Activity (results may vary)<br /> Is It Real? Ghosts and Hauntings<br /> The Others<br /> The Shining (Original, tv film view at your own risk)<br /> Ghostbusters (Original, Paul Fieg film unknown fate)<br /> Carnival of Souls<br /> Children of the Grave<br /> Shadowbound (web series, yep, it's because it was filmed in my hometown)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T22:33:26-07:00","id":927456,"title":"","content":"I recommend talking to paranormal investigators--at least the ones I met really seem to believe the stuff. If nothing else it's an interesting study in psychology.<br /> <br /> Carnivale is great generally but for Wraith I particularly recommend the episode Babylon.<br /> <br /> Hamlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T06:59:09-07:00","id":928091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=926849#post926849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Crow--I think? It's so tonally uncanny I can't bring myself to finish it. In a different mood I think I'd like the atmosphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? What did you find so tonally uncanny?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T19:56:24-07:00","id":928566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=928091#post928091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? What did you find so tonally uncanny?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard to explain. There's a kind of aggression and intensity to a lot of 90's media that comes across as inauthentic to me. Like I said, it could have just been the mood I was in--I'll give it another shot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T00:08:26-07:00","id":928623,"title":"","content":"One important theme of a lot of Wraith games is the tension between the individual and society. The Hierarchy is oppressive and uncompromising and corrupt, yet they are the best hope against Oblivion. Unfortunately I don't know a lot of fiction that deals directly with this kind of thing. The only one I can think of is Antigone by Sophocles. I've heard that nearly all fiction since Shakespeare has focused more on the individual than society. That's probably an overstatement. Maybe Dickens? I haven't read any so I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T11:03:09-07:00","id":928822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=928566#post928566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to explain. There's a kind of aggression and intensity to a lot of 90's media that comes across as inauthentic to me. Like I said, it could have just been the mood I was in--I'll give it another shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that's kind of the point of the story. Nash a couple years ago did <a href=\"http://radiodeadair.com/2013/12/13/here-there-be-dragons-the-crow/\" target=\"_blank\">a great video on the Crow</a> as part of his Here There be Dragons series and he talked about the film's themes.<br /> <br /> The short version of it without spoilers like in Nash's video, the intense violence Erik inflicts on the people who murdered him and Shelly is supposed to be intense and unsettling because that is not who Erik was. His quest for vengeance is driving him away from his humanity, away from everything that he was, becoming akin to the men that destroyed his life. As he's murdering his killers he's killing himself far more than anything anyone else could have done. But the people who knew him and his own memories are trying to pull him back from the brink, to keep him who he was.<br /> <br /> Not unlike the struggle between Psyche and Shadow in a wraith.<br /> <br /> If you don't mind spoilers or have seen the film, watch Nash's review, he described the film's themes far better than I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T05:09:11-07:00","id":929199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=928566#post928566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's hard to explain. There's a kind of aggression and intensity to a lot of 90's media that comes across as inauthentic to me. Like I said, it could have just been the mood I was in--I'll give it another shot.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the oWoD was all about that post-punk, goth-meets-MTV intensity that encapsulates the 90s. It was the decade of the poser with nothing to fight for but the sense that she should fight anyway because she'd grown up on 80s movies and punk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T17:43:11-07:00","id":929463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=929199#post929199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the oWoD was all about that post-punk, goth-meets-MTV intensity that encapsulates the 90s. It was the decade of the poser with nothing to fight for but the sense that she should fight anyway because she'd grown up on 80s movies and punk.</div> </div> </div> </div>I grew up in the 90's, so I know very well what you mean. It sounds like The Crow has good in-story reason for being the way it is though. I'll probably check it out again.<br /> <br /> But, to get back to my last comment--does anyone know many fictional works that get into the conflict between nation/city-state/tribe versus the individual?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T18:10:46-07:00","id":929471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=929463#post929463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, to get back to my last comment--does anyone know many fictional works that get into the conflict between nation/city-state/tribe versus the individual?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I might be missing the mark of your question, but for \u201cgood\u201d stories about individuals against a political core, you could try <i>A Long Way Gone</i> (Beah, 2007) or even \u2013 on NetFlix \u2013 <i>Beasts of No Nation</i> (Fukunaga, 2015). They\u2019re not exactly Dickens, but the parallels of a small and lonely soul being pressed into military service by a [seemingly] monolithic entity are there. I originally read <i>A Long Way Gone</i> for Shovelhead inspiration but found the source material too serious; I couldn\u2019t bring myself to use such inspiration with the irreverence I\u2019m known for in my Sabbat games. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:40:10-07:00","id":929898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=928623#post928623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard that nearly all fiction since Shakespeare has focused more on the individual than society. That's probably an overstatement. Maybe Dickens? I haven't read any so I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... What? No.<br /> <br /> Perhaps you have misinterpreted the claim that<i> individual authors</i> have become more important in modern Western society beginning with the Renaissance? Previously, &quot;stables&quot; of scribes would churn out tales and fancies in a more &quot;assembly line&quot; method. Audiences didn't care about the name of the author so much as the name of the hero of the story, and the role of the author as creator/owner was not held in high regard (famously, Miguel Cervantes wrote about the &quot;unlicensed, unofficial&quot; sequels starring his Knight of the Sorrowful Face in the introduction of the second book of <i>Don Quixote</i>).<br /> <br /> Because I mean... Kafka, right? At the very least. All fiction (all entertainment, really) is reflective of the society that produces it - one cannot separate it. If one says &quot;Oh, but that's just dumb entertainment,&quot; <i>why</i> is it dumb entertainment? Why are those specific things entertaining? &quot;It's just boobs and explosions.&quot; What about our society finds value-as-entertainment in those things? Is it just we like to see things explode? Is there a larger contextual framework?<br /> <br /> Sorry, got a bit off track there. It's summer and I have no papers to grade.<br /> <br /> But to get back to your question, anything can be read as a conflict between the individual and society - <i>Infinite Jest</i> can be read through the lens of an individual trying to protect his tribe from a greater social institution(s). If you're looking for something more narrowly specific, like <i>To Kill a Mockingbird</i>, where one man faces a clearly defined government authority, though I would recommend Kafka again, especially <i>The Trial</i> and <i>The Castle</i> (where the only defining features of the government are their overbearing, inscrutable, and inaccessible methods - they are faceless and monolithic).<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T08:42:43-07:00","id":930364,"title":"","content":"As for the &quot;newness&quot; of the concept of &quot;individual vs. society&quot;, witness <i>The Iliad</i>, Achilles is putting his own desires above the customs and mores of his society. Repeatedly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T09:22:21-07:00","id":930375,"title":"","content":"I've only played Silent Hill 2, but the whole series is ripe for harvesting. The whole experience could be a harrowing. The Otherworld is a fantastic visual for the Underworld. The total disregard for the consistency of the human form is especially relevant for Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T20:08:33-07:00","id":930675,"title":"","content":"I remember back in the mid 90s I attended a panel where Richard Dansky remarked that <i>The Frighteners</i> was basically <i>Wraith: The Motion Picture</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T09:08:07-07:00","id":930891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=930675#post930675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember back in the mid 90s I attended a panel where Richard Dansky remarked that <i>The Frighteners</i> was basically <i>Wraith: The Motion Picture</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda seems a bit more like Mediums/Oracles the Motion Picture or, even, a non-corporate/non-technologized Orpheus the Motion Picture. (Or somewhere in between.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T14:17:47-07:00","id":931021,"title":"","content":"Dare I say the new Ghostbusters without winding up dead? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T14:31:23-07:00","id":931024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=931021#post931021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dare I say the new Ghostbusters without winding up dead? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I'm reserving judgment until I actually see it, but the trailers make it look one, long SNL skit. Here's to hoping for the best...</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T14:55:18-07:00","id":931032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=931024#post931024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I'm reserving judgment until I actually see it, but the trailers make it look one, long SNL skit. Here's to hoping for the best...</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't impressed by the trailers either. If you like Bridesmaids or Spy, you should like it. But even if you don't, there's enough there to like if you're a fan of Ghostbusters the franchise (which, of course, always went beyond the two movies anyway). All the original cast appear at one point or another, which is nice, but it's relatively restrained on the fanwankery compared to, say, the new Star Wars. There are some clever touches (such as how they get their familiar logo and how they end up in their fire station), and enough new stuff to keep it feeling fresh. Plus, Chris Hemsworth steals every scene he's in--his character is a real highlight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T08:53:28-07:00","id":931388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=931032#post931032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't impressed by the trailers either. If you like Bridesmaids or Spy, you should like it. But even if you don't, there's enough there to like if you're a fan of Ghostbusters the franchise (which, of course, always went beyond the two movies anyway). All the original cast appear at one point or another, which is nice, but it's relatively restrained on the fanwankery compared to, say, the new Star Wars. There are some clever touches (such as how they get their familiar logo and how they end up in their fire station), and enough new stuff to keep it feeling fresh. Plus, Chris Hemsworth steals every scene he's in--his character is a real highlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they have an actual cameo by Harold Ramis (Egon), it's REALLY a Wraith-appropriate movie....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T00:15:19-07:00","id":931869,"title":"","content":"If you're a fan of anime, <b>Bleach</b> does a good job showing the dynamics between Psyche (Ichigo), Eidolon (Zangetsu), and Shadow (inner Hollow). <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y83dmIBMRp4\" target=\"_blank\"><u>This scene</u></a> from the big duel between Ichigo and Byakuya (Soul Society arc) is almost a textbook example of Catharsis, for example. On the brink of defeat, wounded and exhausted, with an enemy pushing all of his buttons, something dark and terrible erupts from the depths of Ichigo's soul . . .<br /> <br /> If you have the whole series, pay attention to how radically Ichigo's personality and fighting style shift. Before, he'd been the good natured renegade, looked down upon by society, but always ready to protect his friends and family. His powers and fighting style had a defensive streak to them, allowing him to be anywhere/everywhere, to help everyone at the same time. <br /> <br /> But once the mask appears, and his inner Hollow erupts . . . Its all offense, all power moves. Nothing matters except breaking his opponent, and utterly humiliating them. Which is very much what Ichigo's Shadow would be like, were you to build him using <i>Wraith</i>'s rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T07:51:23-07:00","id":932007,"title":"","content":"My only problem with the new Ghostbusters film, is the fact that it's a reboot. Telling me the first two Ghostbusters never happened, nor the cartoon series, nor the videogames, is something I just can't wrap my head around. They could've easily updated everything, and explained what happened to the original cast. I'll be waiting for it to hit Netflix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T10:04:48-07:00","id":932069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=932007#post932007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only problem with the new Ghostbusters film, is the fact that it's a reboot. Telling me the first two Ghostbusters never happened, nor the cartoon series, nor the videogames, is something I just can't wrap my head around. They could've easily updated everything, and explained what happened to the original cast. I'll be waiting for it to hit Netflix.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not helped by how Sony and Director in particular have treated fans that weren't crazy about the trails.<br /> <br /> At best I might see it at a cheap theatre after opening weekend if the reviews turn out go. But from the reviewers I trust that have come out, it's at best average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T11:44:54-07:00","id":932120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=932069#post932069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not helped by how Sony and Director in particular have treated fans that weren't crazy about the trails.<br /> <br /> At best I might see it at a cheap theatre after opening weekend if the reviews turn out go. But from the reviewers I trust that have come out, it's at best average.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed.<br /> <br /> I have heard that Kate McKinnon is awesome in it(as one of the few bright spots), but like I said, I'm a sucker for continuity. And...well...this just sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T02:22:47-07:00","id":932847,"title":"","content":"EDIT: Pressed enter by mistake...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-17-2016, 05:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T02:31:41-07:00","id":932849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=932120#post932120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Agreed.<br /> <br /> I have heard that Kate McKinnon is awesome in it(as one of the few bright spots), but like I said, I'm a sucker for continuity. And...well...this just sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a reboot, so of course there's no continuity. However, all the old stars do appear (including Ramis, but it's a blink-and-you'll-miss-it moment). I think if they'd gone the way of The Force Awakens and forced in everything the fans wanted, it would have been a much worse film. The Force Awakens was just awful. It was a parade of geriatric stars paying fan service as if at a convention... Like the opening of Galaxy Quest, but without the humour. <br /> <br /> McKinnon is great, as is Hemsworth, but, TBH, the cast is pretty uniformly good. Don't get me wrong, it's far from my favourite film, but the disdain shown by people who haven't even seen it and who just want it to fail has made me more determined to fight its corner. Sometimes fans can just be awful, awful people and there were folks on IMDb giving the movie one star with things like 'I don't want to watch this man-hating evil that has murdered my childhood'. I had to give it a ten-star rating to balance it out just because it seemed like such a ridiculous reaction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-17T11:04:55-07:00","id":932974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=932849#post932849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a reboot, so of course there's no continuity. However, all the old stars do appear (including Ramis, but it's a blink-and-you'll-miss-it moment). I think if they'd gone the way of The Force Awakens and forced in everything the fans wanted, it would have been a much worse film. The Force Awakens was just awful. It was a parade of geriatric stars paying fan service as if at a convention... Like the opening of Galaxy Quest, but without the humour.<br /> <br /> McKinnon is great, as is Hemsworth, but, TBH, the cast is pretty uniformly good. Don't get me wrong, it's far from my favourite film, but the disdain shown by people who haven't even seen it and who just want it to fail has made me more determined to fight its corner. Sometimes fans can just be awful, awful people and there were folks on IMDb giving the movie one star with things like 'I don't want to watch this man-hating evil that has murdered my childhood'. <b>I had to give it a ten-star rating to balance it out just because it seemed like such a ridiculous reaction.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. But the extreme opposite is not the way to go, IMO, and just leads to plenty of unbalanced review scores that tell shit-all about the film. And I know it's a reboot. Which is my problem with it.<br /> <br /> So I'll see it, eventually. Just not in theaters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T01:25:50-07:00","id":933319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=932974#post932974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. But the extreme opposite is not the way to go, IMO, and just leads to plenty of unbalanced review scores that tell shit-all about the film. And I know it's a reboot. Which is my problem with it.<br /> <br /> So I'll see it, eventually. Just not in theaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The score I gave was a 10, but I've always been pretty balanced with the actual things I've said about it, despite that. The 10 was just to balance out the 1s, because when it first came out it had an average rating of 3, which was quite obviously ludicrous. It's a funny film. It's not the best, but then what film is these days? The nature of films has changed. Even IMDb's current rating of 5 or so seems ridiculously low, given the higher ratings of much worse films. In general, I'm with the critical consensus, which is about 7/8, and isn't as emotive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T07:56:50-07:00","id":933418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/925709-is-there-an-inspirational-works-post-for-the-wraith-forum?p=933319#post933319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The score I gave was a 10, but I've always been pretty balanced with the actual things I've said about it, despite that. The 10 was just to balance out the 1s, because when it first came out it had an average rating of 3, which was quite obviously ludicrous. It's a funny film. It's not the best, but then what film is these days? The nature of films has changed. Even IMDb's current rating of 5 or so seems ridiculously low, given the higher ratings of much worse films. In general, <b>I'm with the critical consensus, which is about 7/8,</b> and isn't as emotive.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the feeling I've been getting from friends/acquaintances that have seen it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T08:39:03-07:00","id":990429,"title":"","content":"The Asphyx<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Awiut4dExcA\" data-code=\"Awiut4dExcA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Awiut4dExcA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videoconta